 (PS base64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.\n{\n  \"2db1b9d8-fbb2-4808-aaaa-f0b31bd4a991\": {\n    \"resource-scenario\": \"resource_hijacking\",\n    \"resource-attack\": \"T1496\",\n    \"resource-url\": \"https://5b16a765d4.example.invalid/d547e57913d0.dat\",\n    \"resource-wallet\": \"wallet_fccc8e312c6271c4911e7d68a9361d30\",\n    \"resource-mutex\": \"Global\\\\HuntressLab_0870a75970bf\",\n    \"collection-scenario\": \"synthetic_collection\",\n    \"collection-attack\": \"T1555.003\",\n    \"collection-url\": \"https://922f25c5d3.example.invalid/739f7b232998.dat\",\n    \"collection-file\": \"update-922f25c5d3.dat\",\n    \"collection-user-agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 HuntressLab/6.7\",\n    \"impact-scenario\": \"synthetic_impact\",\n    \"impact-attack\": \"T1486\",\n    \"impact-extension\": \".locked-f3994\",\n    \"impact-note\": \"RECOVERY-f39944fd61.txt\",\n    \"impact-url\": \"https://cdn-f39944fd61.example.inva