{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B8fSf6RicHGZZwNECUxuxh","type":"tool_result","content":"140\t    `console_report`/`typed_array_to_file`/`stream_pipeline`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/\n141\t    process_builder/schedule_builder/operation_graph.\n142\t  - indicators: campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path,\n143\t    schedule_path, service_name. Indicator questions read \"exact X indicator\", where X is the plan key.\n144\t  - per-language labels: batch `graph` (D9 confirmed linear/single/diamond/fan_out/fallback_retry/cross_language/\n145\t    same_language), Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain, Bash feature/primitive, v=3 host_profile/\n146\t    obfuscation_profile/stage_profile/next_language.\n147\t  - v=3 host_profile seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell (D8), sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty\n148\t    (D9), perl_cgi (D15). obfuscation: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex. stage_profile: single_descriptor/\n149\t    two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff.\n150\t  - Bash advanced feature|primitive (always plan-verbatim; 14 seen D7-D14), e.g. indirect_expansion|parameter_indirection,\n151\t    associative_arrays|declare_associative, heredoc_reconstruction|quoted_heredoc, getopts_state|option_parser_state (D14),\n152\t    brace_expansion|cartesian_brace_expansion (D14). Family = `bash-advanced-<file-stem>` (D7 short forms: `indirect`, `tokens`).\n153\t  - **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT technique ids: `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain -- PHP, WSF,\n154\t    HTA, SCT, Lua alike) and `T1053` (persistence_descriptor), NOT the host-language sub-technique. The role->ATT&CK table\n155\t    below is for v=1/v=2 plans only. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14 MSBuild: benign_utility had steps\n156\t    `decode_embedded>write_file>dispatch_process`, launcher `decode_configuration>return_configuration`) -- copy role= and steps=\n157\t    independently; never \"fix\" one from the other.\n158\t- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 plans; v=3 states `role=`):\n159\t\n160\t  | steps | role |\n161\t  |---|---|\n162\t  | decode_configuration,return_configuration | benign_utility |\n163\t  | acquire_remote + dispatch_memory/dispatch_pipe | stager |\n164\t  | acquire_remote,write_file | downloader |\n165\t  | decode_embedded,write_file | dropper |\n166\t  | locate_local,dispatch_process | launcher |\n167\t  | read_file/upload,transmit_remote | uploader |\n168\t  | transform + recovery_note | impact |\n169\t  | build_schedule,register_descriptor (Node d7) | persistence_descriptor |\n170\t  | recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + plan `feature=` (Bash d7-d9) | advanced_syntax |\n171\t  | ends in handoff_script (JS/Batch/VBS) or profile_host..dispatch_process | staged_chain |\n172\t  | dispatch_next_stage (Python) | relay |\n173\t\n174\t  cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.\n175\t- **Role -> ATT&CK** (GM-confirmed d2-d9; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)` has the table):\n176\t  - benign `none`; downloader and stager T1105; dropper T1140; uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor\n177\t    T1053.003 (by role, whatever the adapter); advanced_syntax T1059.004.\n178\t  - launcher/staged_chain/relay follow the HOST LANGUAGE: T1059.003 batch, .004 bash, .005 VBS, .006 python, .007\n179\t    JScript AND Node.js (.001 PS predicted, never asked).\n180\t  - PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496, synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486.\n181\t  - REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001); stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.\n182\t- **Batch expansion** (closed set; mined from EVERY GM-verified D3-D6 case, 0 conflicts in 545):\n183\t  - fragments named `h<N>` AND joined with `call set` (bare, or `for %%G in (..) do call set`) = `call_double`\n184\t  - `for %%G in (..) do call set \"cfg=%%cfg%%%%<pool>%%G%%\"` over any OTHER pool (v_a/item/fragment/FrAg) = `for_indirect`\n185\t  - everything else = `delayed`, INCLUDING h-pools joined with `!h0!!h1!..` (the \"h-pool = call_double\" shortcut failed).\n186\t  - Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%...\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9 -- skip `set` lines whose\n187\t    value references the other fragments (a wrong Mastery answer on D6).\n188\t  - D13+ question text: \"Classify only the expansion form used by the descriptor reconstruction statement\" with enum\n189\t    percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect. In the `run_for_time:false` pool the label follows that wording literally\n190\t    (statement-only table under Variant axes); single solve still followed the echo(!var!) rules above.\n191\t  - REJECTED: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n192\t- **Batch control**: direct (separator lines and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control), errorlevel_guard\n193\t  (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine, if_guard (`if defined X`). REJECTED:\n194\t  linear, straight_line, sequential, goto, goto_label, double_pipe, pipe, ampersand, call_label, dead_label, errorlevel,\n195\t  opaque_branch, + ~40 \"if defined\" synonyms.\n196\t- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`),\n197\t  for_once. REJECTED: do_loop, do_exit, while_wend, while_loop, on_error_resume.\n198\t- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 copied VERBATIM; spellings differ per\n199\t  language (Python `decimal_csv`, batch `decimal_bytes|reverse_xor`): read the const, never translate.\n200\t- **JScript styles** (closed sets in the question text; GM-confirmed D2-D9):\n201\t  - function-style: `function f(` = declaration; `var f = function(` = anonymous_expression; `var f = function f_body(` = named_expression.\n202\t  - invocation-style: how recover/inspect invokes the next top-level function: `f(x)` = direct, `f.call(..)` (also via\n203\t    a local `invoke` helper doing `block.call`) = call, `f.apply(..)` = apply.\n204\t  - property-style: only `o.k` = dot, only `o[\"k\"]` = bracket_literal, both = mixed. triage's `shape:` line counts them.\n205\t- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli). Compose unknown labels from the SHORT language keyword:\n206\t  - conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`.\n207\t  - The spelled-out statement (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit, while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, defined_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected.\n208\t\n209\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n210\t- **Diffing bytes when the regime changed** (D15 Mastery, ~5 min): 25 batch-expansion ids flipped delayed->percent on\n211\t  byte-identical files. Tabulate (join shape, pool, GM label) per contract metadata key at once; `localize` found the\n212\t  value in one pass, the generalize workers took several hypotheses to find `run_for_time:false`.\n213\t- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h and two fields hit the 6-wrong cap on `if defined`. Apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates from lib/playbook.py.\n214\t- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the whole batch; `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s). Probe uncertain label fields ONE per submit; the wrong cap is per field.\n215\t- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1 collection, d2 launcher/stager/dropper): use the role->ATT&CK table. Adapter names (regsvr32, systemd_descriptor) do NOT change the technique.\n216\t  Exception: a plan that states `attack=` (v=3) is authoritative even when it is a parent id (T1059, T1053).\n217\t- **Routing by file extension** (D8-D9): `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT-scriptlet markup and `.vbs` held a WSF job with\n218\t  VBScript+JScript. Check for the plan marker first; use the extension only as a fallback. Marker-first routing is why\n219\t  the D8 solver needed no change on D9.\n220\t- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids lost on the 1st submit): new family names contain hyphens\n221\t  (`bash-advanced-associative-arrays-feature`, `polyglot-php-persistence-descriptor-stage-profile`). Resolve the field\n222\t  as the longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`), not by a prefix-strip regex.\n223\t- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT 26b7da83, one timed attempt lost): `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B)\n224\t  landed as `evidence.zip`, so every field came out None/default and the submit failed. Before solving or diagnosing,\n225\t  check artifact size + sha256 against the start response (`artifacts[].sha256`, or the `[assigned-artifact-sha256:..]`\n226\t  tag in timed question texts). A tiny JSON `{\"error\":..}` = transport failure (retry the download), NOT a variant.\n227\t  Solvers should exit non-zero on it (the D7-D9 solver does). Don't harvest it as a regression case.\n228\t- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D15 `solver/NOTES.md` is still the D7 copy; D15's regime fix lives only in a\n229\t  solve.py comment). Date every VARIANT AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n230\t- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT: 15 ids unanswered). Fall back to material-shape readings x the\n231\t  named transform; never let an unknown NAME stop the decode.\n232\t- **cmd arg parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`. CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur.\n233\t- **Bash Codec key**: comma-separated multi-byte keys parsed as contiguous hex give key [0] (`lib.scripts.codec_key()`).\n234\t  **stage_count != len(steps)** (d6): read the plan field.\n235\t- **Timed modes are a transport race.** D2 Mastery expired (downloads ate 4-5 s of 6 s; sets submitted serially). D7 TT\n236\t  spent 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving (start 3.9, download 3.1, submit 6.0); D8-D9 transport was fast (start 0.6-1.5 s,\n237\t  download 0.3-1.3 s). Solver ~0.2-4 s (D9 Mastery: 5 sets in 1.8 s, forked per set); submit all sets in one call.\n238\t- **Same-name deliveries.** Pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered rather than\n239\t  reuse set 1's members (confidently wrong 42-174 times in regression cases).\n240\t- **Re-walking nested AES zips per question** cost ~1.3 s (903 PBKDF2 runs). Index the tree once, and don't decrypt\n241\t  script leaves to sniff for a nested zip (keep the leaf-extension list current: `.lua` missing D9; still missing on D14:\n242\t  `.lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj` -- speed only, solve stayed ~1 s).\n243\t- **Never execute fixtures.** Every decode so far worked from the Codec const plus a restricted interpreter of the\n244\t  Load/Decode bodies. Cross-check two decoders; accept a plan only if it parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n245\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64eedee1-889a-4eb5-b636-2a20820e2d49","uuid":"a83ca799-4e38-48e1-82cd-2a584401b81c","timestamp":"2026-10-15T13:09:33.292Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"    `console_report`/`typed_array_to_file`/`stream_pipeline`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/\n    process_builder/schedule_builder/operation_graph.\n  - indicators: campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path,\n    schedule_path, service_name. Indicator questions read \"exact X indicator\", where X is the plan key.\n  - per-language labels: batch `graph` (D9 confirmed linear/single/diamond/fan_out/fallback_retry/cross_language/\n    same_language), Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain, Bash feature/primitive, v=3 host_profile/\n    obfuscation_profile/stage_profile/next_language.\n  - v=3 host_profile seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell (D8), sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty\n    (D9), perl_cgi (D15). obfuscation: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex. stage_profile: single_descriptor/\n    two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff.\n  - Bash advanced feature|primitive (always plan-verbatim; 14 seen D7-D14), e.g. indirect_expansion|parameter_indirection,\n    associative_arrays|declare_associative, heredoc_reconstruction|quoted_heredoc, getopts_state|option_parser_state (D14),\n    brace_expansion|cartesian_brace_expansion (D14). Family = `bash-advanced-<file-stem>` (D7 short forms: `indirect`, `tokens`).\n  - **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT technique ids: `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain -- PHP, WSF,\n    HTA, SCT, Lua alike) and `T1053` (persistence_descriptor), NOT the host-language sub-technique. The role->ATT&CK table\n    below is for v=1/v=2 plans only. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14 MSBuild: benign_utility had steps\n    `decode_embedded>write_file>dispatch_process`, launcher `decode_configuration>return_configuration`) -- copy role= and steps=\n    independently; never \"fix\" one from the other.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 plans; v=3 states `role=`):\n\n  | steps | role |\n  |---|---|\n  | decode_configuration,return_configuration | benign_utility |\n  | acquire_remote + dispatch_memory/dispatch_pipe | stager |\n  | acquire_remote,write_file | downloader |\n  | decode_embedded,write_file | dropper |\n  | locate_local,dispatch_process | launcher |\n  | read_file/upload,transmit_remote | uploader |\n  | transform + recovery_note | impact |\n  | build_schedule,register_descriptor (Node d7) | persistence_descriptor |\n  | recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + plan `feature=` (Bash d7-d9) | advanced_syntax |\n  | ends in handoff_script (JS/Batch/VBS) or profile_host..dispatch_process | staged_chain |\n  | dispatch_next_stage (Python) | relay |\n\n  cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (GM-confirmed d2-d9; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)` has the table):\n  - benign `none`; downloader and stager T1105; dropper T1140; uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor\n    T1053.003 (by role, whatever the adapter); advanced_syntax T1059.004.\n  - launcher/staged_chain/relay follow the HOST LANGUAGE: T1059.003 batch, .004 bash, .005 VBS, .006 python, .007\n    JScript AND Node.js (.001 PS predicted, never asked).\n  - PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496, synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486.\n  - REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001); stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.\n- **Batch expansion** (closed set; mined from EVERY GM-verified D3-D6 case, 0 conflicts in 545):\n  - fragments named `h<N>` AND joined with `call set` (bare, or `for %%G in (..) do call set`) = `call_double`\n  - `for %%G in (..) do call set \"cfg=%%cfg%%%%<pool>%%G%%\"` over any OTHER pool (v_a/item/fragment/FrAg) = `for_indirect`\n  - everything else = `delayed`, INCLUDING h-pools joined with `!h0!!h1!..` (the \"h-pool = call_double\" shortcut failed).\n  - Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%...\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9 -- skip `set` lines whose\n    value references the other fragments (a wrong Mastery answer on D6).\n  - D13+ question text: \"Classify only the expansion form used by the descriptor reconstruction statement\" with enum\n    percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect. In the `run_for_time:false` pool the label follows that wording literally\n    (statement-only table under Variant axes); single solve still followed the echo(!var!) rules above.\n  - REJECTED: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct (separator lines and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control), errorlevel_guard\n  (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine, if_guard (`if defined X`). REJECTED:\n  linear, straight_line, sequential, goto, goto_label, double_pipe, pipe, ampersand, call_label, dead_label, errorlevel,\n  opaque_branch, + ~40 \"if defined\" synonyms.\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`),\n  for_once. REJECTED: do_loop, do_exit, while_wend, while_loop, on_error_resume.\n- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 copied VERBATIM; spellings differ per\n  language (Python `decimal_csv`, batch `decimal_bytes|reverse_xor`): read the const, never translate.\n- **JScript styles** (closed sets in the question text; GM-confirmed D2-D9):\n  - function-style: `function f(` = declaration; `var f = function(` = anonymous_expression; `var f = function f_body(` = named_expression.\n  - invocation-style: how recover/inspect invokes the next top-level function: `f(x)` = direct, `f.call(..)` (also via\n    a local `invoke` helper doing `block.call`) = call, `f.apply(..)` = apply.\n  - property-style: only `o.k` = dot, only `o[\"k\"]` = bracket_literal, both = mixed. triage's `shape:` line counts them.\n- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli). Compose unknown labels from the SHORT language keyword:\n  - conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`.\n  - The spelled-out statement (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit, while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, defined_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Diffing bytes when the regime changed** (D15 Mastery, ~5 min): 25 batch-expansion ids flipped delayed->percent on\n  byte-identical files. Tabulate (join shape, pool, GM label) per contract metadata key at once; `localize` found the\n  value in one pass, the generalize workers took several hypotheses to find `run_for_time:false`.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h and two fields hit the 6-wrong cap on `if defined`. Apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates from lib/playbook.py.\n- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the whole batch; `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s). Probe uncertain label fields ONE per submit; the wrong cap is per field.\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1 collection, d2 launcher/stager/dropper): use the role->ATT&CK table. Adapter names (regsvr32, systemd_descriptor) do NOT change the technique.\n  Exception: a plan that states `attack=` (v=3) is authoritative even when it is a parent id (T1059, T1053).\n- **Routing by file extension** (D8-D9): `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT-scriptlet markup and `.vbs` held a WSF job with\n  VBScript+JScript. Check for the plan marker first; use the extension only as a fallback. Marker-first routing is why\n  the D8 solver needed no change on D9.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids lost on the 1st submit): new family names contain hyphens\n  (`bash-advanced-associative-arrays-feature`, `polyglot-php-persistence-descriptor-stage-profile`). Resolve the field\n  as the longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`), not by a prefix-strip regex.\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT 26b7da83, one timed attempt lost): `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B)\n  landed as `evidence.zip`, so every field came out None/default and the submit failed. Before solving or diagnosing,\n  check artifact size + sha256 against the start response (`artifacts[].sha256`, or the `[assigned-artifact-sha256:..]`\n  tag in timed question texts). A tiny JSON `{\"error\":..}` = transport failure (retry the download), NOT a variant.\n  Solvers should exit non-zero on it (the D7-D9 solver does). Don't harvest it as a regression case.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D15 `solver/NOTES.md` is still the D7 copy; D15's regime fix lives only in a\n  solve.py comment). Date every VARIANT AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT: 15 ids unanswered). Fall back to material-shape readings x the\n  named transform; never let an unknown NAME stop the decode.\n- **cmd arg parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`. CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur.\n- **Bash Codec key**: comma-separated multi-byte keys parsed as contiguous hex give key [0] (`lib.scripts.codec_key()`).\n  **stage_count != len(steps)** (d6): read the plan field.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race.** D2 Mastery expired (downloads ate 4-5 s of 6 s; sets submitted serially). D7 TT\n  spent 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving (start 3.9, download 3.1, submit 6.0); D8-D9 transport was fast (start 0.6-1.5 s,\n  download 0.3-1.3 s). Solver ~0.2-4 s (D9 Mastery: 5 sets in 1.8 s, forked per set); submit all sets in one call.\n- **Same-name deliveries.** Pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered rather than\n  reuse set 1's members (confidently wrong 42-174 times in regression cases).\n- **Re-walking nested AES zips per question** cost ~1.3 s (903 PBKDF2 runs). Index the tree once, and don't decrypt\n  script leaves to sniff for a nested zip (keep the leaf-extension list current: `.lua` missing D9; still missing on D14:\n  `.lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj` -- speed only, solve stayed ~1 s).\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Every decode so far worked from the Codec const plus a restricted interpreter of the\n  Load/Decode bodies. Cross-check two decoders; accept a plan only if it parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n","numLines":106,"startLine":140,"totalLines":245}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B8fSf6RicHGZZwNECUxuxh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
